      "page_title": "Healthchecks, Tier Splits & Teardown",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Waiting Properly"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`depends_on` waits for start, never for readiness.",
            "Pair it with a `healthcheck` and `condition: service_healthy`.",
            "Otherwise the app dials a database that isn't listening yet."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Frontend / Backend Split",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "networks:",
            "  front:",
            "  back:",
            "    internal: true  # no way out",
            "services:",
            "  db: {networks: [back]}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Attach each service with its own `networks:` list.",
            "The proxy joins both; the database joins only `back`.",
            "Long syntax (`type:`, `source:`, `target:`) for real mounts."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "One Door In",
          "text": "Only the reverse proxy gets `ports:`. The data tier lives on an `internal` network with nothing published."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Two Patterns Worth Stealing",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Base file mounts nothing; override adds source bind + hot reload.",
            "Production runs the base file alone.",
            "`network_mode: host` kills Compose networking and voids `ports:`."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "volumes:",
            "  - ./app:/app",
            "  - /app/node_modules   # anon vol shields it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "Removes"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "down",
              "containers + network"
            ],
            [
              "down -v",
              "also named + anonymous volumes"
            ],
            [
              "down --remove-orphans",
              "deleted services"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Debug Step One"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker inspect c   # read .NetworkSettings",
            "#                  # and .Mounts",
            "docker port c      # published, for real",
            "ss -ltnp           # host is listening?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Meant vs Wired",
          "text": "`inspect` shows what actually got wired. Your compose file only shows what you meant to wire."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Triage: Refused, Timeout & Stale Mounts",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Refused Versus Timeout",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Symptom",
            "Likely cause"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Refused / reset from host",
              "app bound to 127.0.0.1"
            ],
            [
              "Name fails between containers",
              "different networks"
            ],
            [
              "Refused, right net",
              "used host port, not real one"
            ],
            [
              "Timeout",
              "firewall, routing, MTU"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Netshoot In The Namespace",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker run --rm -it \\",
            "  --network container:web \\",
            "  nicolaka/netshoot",
            "# dig, ss, tcpdump in its netns"
          ],
          "note": "for scratch and distroless images"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Debug Order",
          "text": "`inspect` → listening on 0.0.0.0? → same network? → firewall or MTU → `netshoot` inside the target's namespace."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The Whole Model",
          "text": "The image is the code, the network is the wiring, the volume is the state. Keep the three apart and containers stay disposable."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Stale Files, Full Disks"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The path is shadowed by another mount on top of it.",
            "The volume was seeded once and is now stale.",
            "The build COPYed the file to a different directory.",
            "`docker system df -v`: dangling volumes eat the disk."
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "Your container can't be reached and your database just vanished — a network namespace gave it a private network, and its writable layer dies with the container. Part 3 of DOCKER NETWORKING & VOLUMES covers healthchecks that gate startup, splitting front and back tiers, what `down -v` really deletes, and a triage table for refused, timeout and stale mounts. Save it before the next Permission denied.",
